    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_Unreadable">That isn't an ISO 8601 date, time, duration or interval.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadYear">The year must be 0001 or later.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadMonth">The month must be 01 to 12.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadDay">That day doesn't exist in that month.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadWeek">That year doesn't have that week number (52 or 53 weeks).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadWeekday">The weekday must be 1 (Monday) to 7 (Sunday).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadOrdinal">That year doesn't have that day number (365 or 366 days).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadHour">The hour must be 00 to 23 (24:00:00 only as the end of a day).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadMinute">The minutes must be 00 to 59.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadSecond">The seconds must be 00 to 60 (60 is a leap second).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_BadOffset">The offset must be Z or +/-hh:mm with hours up to 23 and minutes up to 59.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_OutOfRange">That moment is outside the years a computer can show (1 to 9999).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_EmptyDuration">A duration needs at least one amount, like P1D or PT5M (and nothing after a T that has no time part).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_FractionNotLast">Only the last, smallest amount of a duration may have a fraction.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_FractionalCalendarUnits">Years and months in an interval must be whole numbers.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_ReducedWithTime">A year or a year-and-month alone can't be followed by a time.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_DateTimeTool_IsoProblem_SpaceSeparator">ISO 8601 separates the date and time with T, not a space.</system:String>
