    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_NavShortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_NavVault">Password vault</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_VaultTitle">Password vault</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_VaultIntro">The vault locks itself when you stop using the app for this long. The badge in the vault shows the time left.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Shortcuts_Title">Keyboard shortcuts</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Shortcuts_Intro">Click a key box, then press the keys you want. Global shortcuts work from anywhere in Windows (they need Ctrl, Alt or Win); the others work while Smart Tools is in front. Backspace clears a shortcut, Esc cancels.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Shortcuts_GlobalSwitch">Turn on global shortcuts</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Shortcuts_GlobalSwitchTip">Master switch for every shortcut that works outside Smart Tools.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_BackgroundHeader">Background and startup</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardBackground">Start recording when Smart Tools opens</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardBackgroundTip">Clipboard History records from the moment Smart Tools starts, even if you never open the tool. When this is off, recording starts the first time you open the tool.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_NavClipboard">Clipboard history</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_NavTextRecognition">Text recognition</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngine">Screen OCR engine</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngineHint">Choose the program that reads text for Screen OCR. Windows OCR is the default. Tesseract can read many more languages and doesn't need Windows language packs.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngineWindows">Windows OCR</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngineWindowsTip">The OCR built into Windows. It reads the languages installed in Windows.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngineTesseract">Tesseract</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrEngineTesseractTip">An open-source OCR program that comes with Smart Tools. It reads the languages you install below.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrTesseractMissing">Tesseract isn't in this copy of Smart Tools, so Screen OCR will ask you to switch back to Windows OCR.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrTesseractNote">Reads the languages you install below. Nothing leaves your PC, and only the language downloads use the internet.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrWindowsNote">Reads the languages installed in Windows. Nothing leaves your PC.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrLanguages">Tesseract languages</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_OcrLanguagesHint">Install the languages you need. Each one is a small download (about 1 to 5 MB). English comes with Smart Tools.</system:String>
