    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardRecording">Recording</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardRecordingHint">Choose when Clipboard History starts recording what you copy. Copies marked private, like the Password Vault's, are never recorded. If the tool wasn't opened and history isn't being saved, turning this off clears the list, including pinned items.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardSaved">Saved history</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_ClipboardSavedHint">By default the history lives in memory and is gone when Smart Tools closes. Turn this on to keep it for good. The saved file is encrypted with your Windows account, so other people and other PCs can't read it, but programs you run as yourself could. Pictures over 5 MB are not saved unless you pin them.</system:String>
