    <!--  Settings › Translation languages  -->
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_NavTranslate">Translation languages</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateHeader">Translation models</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateHint">Translate works offline with one downloaded model for each language pair. Download the pairs you need here, or remove them to free disk space.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateLocation">Models are stored in</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateCopyPath">Copy the folder path</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateOpenFailed">Couldn't open the folder.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslatePathCopied">Path copied.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateCopyFailed">Couldn't copy. Another app is using the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateInstalledCount">{0} installed</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateDiskSize">{0} MB on disk</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateDownloadSize">About {0} MB to download</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateDownloading">Downloading… {0}%</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateRemoveFailed">Couldn't delete the model files. Close anything using them (a translation may be running) and try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateForgetTip">Take this pair off the list and delete its downloaded model</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateAddHeader">Add another language pair</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateAddHint">Models usually translate to or from English. If the pair you want doesn't exist, translate in two steps through English. Nothing is downloaded until you press Download.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateHowHeader">How to add a language</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateStep1">1. Click a language below to fill the first box (the language you translate from), then click another one to fill the second box (the language you translate to).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateStep2">2. Press Add pair. Smart Tools checks that a ready-made model exists on Hugging Face.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateStep3">3. Press Download on the new row in the list above, and wait for it to finish. It's about 100 MB, once.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateStep4">4. Open Translate and pick the pair. From then on it works offline.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateCodesHeader">Language codes (left click for From, right click for To)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateCodesNote">You can also type a language name, like chinese or japanese. Chinese is zh, and Japanese is ja.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateChipTip">Left click to use as From, right click to use as To</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateColLanguage">Language</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateColCode">Code</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateAddButton">Add pair</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateChecking">Checking Hugging Face…</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Settings_TranslateAdded">Added {0} to {1}. Download it below, then pick it in Translate.</system:String>

    <!--  Guided tours for the tools added later  -->
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Input_Title">What to copy</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Input_Text">Drop files and folders here. Folders are copied with everything inside, including empty subfolders.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Destination_Title">Where it goes</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Destination_Text">Choose the destination folder. In Move mode this card becomes Move to and remembers its own folder.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Options_Title">Copy or move</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Options_Text">Copy keeps the originals. Move removes each original only after its copy has been checked. Choose what happens when a different file has the same name; nothing is ever overwritten.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Start_Title">Start the queue</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Start_Text">Starts copying. The same button becomes Stop. Files that are already there and identical are recognised and skipped.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Pause_Title">Pause and resume</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Pause_Text">Pauses the queue between blocks so nothing is left half-done, and carries on from the same spot when you resume.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Results_Title">Progress per file</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CopyQueue_Results_Text">Every file shows its state: waiting, copying, verifying, done, already there, skipped or failed. Hover a failed row for the reason.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Input_Title">Folder to export</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Input_Text">Choose the folder whose structure you want. It is only read; nothing in it is changed.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Format_Title">Format</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Format_Text">Pick a text tree, Markdown, JSON or CSV. Changing the format re-writes the same scan without reading the folder again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Options_Title">What to list</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Options_Text">Limit the depth, leave out files, show sizes and dates, include hidden items, or skip folders like .git and node_modules.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Build_Title">Build the tree</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Build_Text">Reads the folder and builds the tree. Press it again while it runs to stop.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Preview_Title">The tree</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FolderTree_Preview_Text">Copy it or save it with the buttons above. Ctrl + mouse wheel changes the text size. Saving never replaces an earlier file.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Input_Title">Audio files</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Input_Text">Drop audio files or whole folders. They are only read while measuring.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Target_Title">Target loudness</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Target_Text">Pick a goal such as YouTube, Spotify or podcast, or your own value, and the highest peak allowed. Changing it only re-judges what was measured.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Output_Title">Where copies go</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Output_Text">Normalized copies are saved here, or next to each original. They are named name (normalized) and never replace a file.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Measure_Title">Measure</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Measure_Text">Reads every file and reports loudness (LUFS), true peak and range. Nothing is written.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Normalize_Title">Normalize copies</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Normalize_Text">Writes a copy of each file brought to your target, then measures the copy again so you see what you really got. Originals stay untouched.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Results_Title">Results</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Loudness_Results_Text">Each file shows its loudness, peak, range, the difference from the target and a verdict: on target, too loud, too quiet or may clip.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_ThisPc_Title">This PC</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_ThisPc_Text">Shows your Wi-Fi adapter and the network you are connected to, with its standard and link speed.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_View_Title">Nearby or saved</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_View_Text">Nearby lists the networks around you with a channel graph per band. Saved lists the networks Windows remembers.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Scan_Title">Scan</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Scan_Text">Listens for networks. It never connects to anything or changes settings. Turn on auto-scan to refresh every 5 seconds.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Channels_Title">Channel graph</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Channels_Text">Each hill is a network on its channel, as tall as its signal. Overlapping hills slow each other down; the green marker is the least crowded channel.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Networks_Title">Access points</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Wifi_Networks_Text">Signal, channel, band, Wi-Fi standard, security and the access point's maker for every network heard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Files_Title">Your media</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Files_Text">Drop pictures, videos and audio, or whole folders, to build the queue.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Order_Title">Play order</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Order_Text">Sequential plays in order, Shuffle mixes the queue and Loop starts again after the last item.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Slideshow_Title">Slideshow</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Slideshow_Text">Choose how many seconds each picture stays on screen.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Keyboard_Title">Keyboard</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Keyboard_Text">The keys that control playback, skipping and the slideshow.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Queue_Title">The queue</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaViewer_Queue_Text">Double-click an item to play it. Right-click for more actions.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Files_Title">Your audio</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Files_Text">Drop audio files or folders to build the playlist.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Mode_Title">Replay mode</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Mode_Text">Choose how the playlist advances, such as in order or shuffled.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Playlist_Title">The playlist</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Playlist_Text">Double-click a track to play it. Tick tracks to act on several at once.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Files_Title">Your pictures</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Files_Text">Drop pictures or folders to build the queue.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Browse_Title">Browse</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Browse_Text">In order goes through the list as it is. Shuffle shows every image once in a random order, then mixes again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Slideshow_Title">Slideshow</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Slideshow_Text">Set the time per picture and start an automatic slideshow.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Keyboard_Title">Keyboard</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Keyboard_Text">The keys for moving between pictures, zooming and the slideshow.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Queue_Title">The queue</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageViewer_Queue_Text">Double-click a picture to open it. Right-click for more actions.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Capture_Title">Capture</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Capture_Text">Choose Area, Window or Screen (every monitor), add a timer if you need to open a menu first, then press Take screenshot.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_MarkUp_Title">Mark up</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_MarkUp_Text">Draw on the picture before saving: pen, arrow, rectangle, highlight, text, or blocks to hide something.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Copy_Title">Copy</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Copy_Text">Copies the picture to the clipboard, ready to paste.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Save_Title">Save</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Screenshot_Save_Text">Saves the picture to a file. An existing file is never replaced.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Device_Title">Microphone</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Device_Text">Choose which microphone to test. Press refresh after plugging one in.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Listen_Title">Listen to yourself</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Listen_Text">Plays the microphone back so you can hear it. Use headphones to avoid feedback.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Start_Title">Start the test</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Start_Text">Shows the live level, the peak and whether the sound clips while you talk.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Device_Title">Camera</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Device_Text">Choose which camera to test. Press refresh after plugging one in.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Start_Title">Start the camera</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Start_Text">Shows the camera live with its resolution, frame rate and brightness, and lets you take a snapshot.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Languages_Title">Languages</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Languages_Text">Choose From and To. The swap button also moves the translation back into the input.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Model_Title">Language model</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Model_Text">A translation model is downloaded the first time a language pair is used; this shows its state.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Run_Title">Translate</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Run_Text">Translates the text on the left.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Copy_Title">Copy the result</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Translate_Copy_Text">Copies the translation to the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Input_Title">Your pictures</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Input_Text">Drop the pictures that will become textures.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Pack_Title">Pack details</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Pack_Text">Name the pack, describe it and set the Minecraft version it is for.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Output_Title">Where it is saved</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Output_Text">The finished pack is saved here and never replaces an existing one.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Run_Title">Build the pack</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_Run_Text">Creates the texture pack from your pictures.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_List_Title">Textures</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TexturePack_List_Text">Every picture and the texture it becomes.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Pairs_Title">Quick pairs</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Pairs_Text">Click a pair of colours to try it straight away.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Rules_Title">What passes</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Rules_Text">Step by step: what the ratio means, why 4.5 : 1 is the line for normal text, and when 3 : 1 or 7 : 1 apply.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Preview_Title">Live preview</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Preview_Text">See the text and background colours together exactly as they will look.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Checks_Title">WCAG checks</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ContrastChecker_Checks_Text">Each check shows the contrast ratio and whether it passes.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Examples_Title">Examples</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Examples_Text">Click an example to fill the box. Type an address with a prefix like 192.168.1.10/24, or with a mask.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Split_Title">Split</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Split_Text">Divide the network into smaller subnets by choosing a new prefix.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Details_Title">Details</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Details_Text">Network, mask, range, broadcast and host count, for IPv4 and IPv6.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Copy_Title">Copy</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_SubnetCalc_Copy_Text">Copies every value to the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Digits_Title">Digits</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Digits_Text">How many digits each code has. Most services use 6.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Period_Title">New code every</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Period_Text">How often the code changes. Most services use 30 seconds.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Algorithm_Title">Algorithm</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Algorithm_Text">The hashing method. Leave SHA-1 unless a service tells you otherwise.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Copy_Title">Copy the code</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Copy_Text">Copies the current code to the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Next_Title">Next code</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Totp_Next_Text">The code that comes after this one, so you can see it in advance.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Kind_Title">What to make</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Kind_Text">Choose UUID v4 (random), UUID v7 or ULID (both sorted by time), random hex, or Lorem ipsum text.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Options_Title">Options</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Options_Text">How many to make and how they look.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Generate_Title">Generate</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Generate_Text">Makes new values with your settings.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Copy_Title">Copy</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IdGenerator_Copy_Text">Copies everything to the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Mode_Title">Mode</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Mode_Text">Choose between a stopwatch, a countdown timer and a Pomodoro cycle.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Start_Title">Start</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Start_Text">Starts, pauses and resumes the clock.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Laps_Title">Laps</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Laps_Text">Each lap you mark is listed with its time.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Direction_Title">Direction</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Direction_Text">Choose CSV to JSON or JSON to CSV.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Options_Title">Options</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Options_Text">Pick the separator or let it be detected, say whether the first row is the header, and keep numbers like 007 as text.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Input_Title">Your data</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Input_Text">Paste or type the data to convert.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Output_Title">The result</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Output_Text">The converted data appears here as you type.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Copy_Title">Copy</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_CsvJson_Copy_Text">Copies the result to the clipboard.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Input_Title">Folders to check</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Input_Text">Add the folders to look through. Only folders with nothing inside count as empty.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Info_Title">Good to know</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Info_Text">Found folders go to the Recycle Bin, never straight to deletion.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Found_Title">Empty folders</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Found_Text">Tick the ones to remove. Nothing is deleted until you confirm.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Actions_Title">Actions</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Actions_Text">Read the battery again, or make Windows' own detailed battery report and open it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_About_Title">About the numbers</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_About_Text">How to read design capacity, full-charge capacity and charge cycles.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Refresh_Title">Refresh</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Refresh_Text">Reads the battery again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Picture_Title">Picture</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Picture_Text">Choose the picture that will become the icon.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Shape_Title">Fit or fill</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Shape_Text">Fit keeps the whole picture inside the square. Fill covers the square and crops what sticks out.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Sizes_Title">Sizes in the .ico</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Sizes_Text">Tick the sizes to include. Windows picks the best one for each place.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Zoom_Title">Zoom</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Zoom_Text">Turn the mouse wheel over the preview to zoom and drag to reposition.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Save_Title">Save the icon</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_IconMaker_Save_Text">Saves the .ico file. An existing file is never replaced.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Input_Title">Your pictures</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Input_Text">Drop the pictures to turn into pixel art.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Pixels_Title">Pixels</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Pixels_Text">How many pixels across the result has (4 to 256). Fewer pixels means chunkier art.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Colors_Title">Colors</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Colors_Text">Pick a palette and how many colours to keep, and turn on dither for smoother gradients.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Save_Title">Save size</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Save_Text">Make each pixel several screen pixels wide so the art stays sharp when enlarged, and add text to the file names.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Output_Title">Where it is saved</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Output_Text">Results are saved here and never replace an existing file.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Convert_Title">Convert all</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_ImageToPixel_Convert_Text">Turns every picture into pixel art.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Beat_Title">Beat</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Beat_Text">Set the beats per bar and whether the first beat gets an accent.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Volume_Title">Volume</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Volume_Text">How loud the click is.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Keys_Title">Keys</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Keys_Text">Space starts and stops. Up and Down change the tempo by 1; hold Ctrl to change it by 10.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Start_Title">Start</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Start_Text">Starts and stops the metronome.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Tempo_Title">Tempo</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Metronome_Tempo_Text">Drag to set the beats per minute.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Input_Title">Your videos</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Input_Text">Drop the videos to take frames from.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Frames_Title">Which frames</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Frames_Text">One frame at a time, exact moments you pick on the slider, or one every few seconds.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Output_Title">Where frames go</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Output_Text">Pictures are saved here and never replace an existing file.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Run_Title">Extract</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_Run_Text">Saves the frames as pictures.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_List_Title">Videos</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_FrameExtractor_List_Text">Pick a video to choose a moment and see the frames saved.</system:String>

    <!--  Extra guided-tour steps  -->
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_Summary_Title">Summary</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_Summary_Text">How many drives were found and how many are healthy, need attention or are unhealthy.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_Admin_Title">Administrator rights</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_Admin_Text">Some SMART details can only be read as administrator. This shows whether the app has them.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Keyboard_Title">Keyboard test</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Keyboard_Text">Press keys to light them up on the map. It counts how many you hold at once to show your rollover, and flags keys that chatter.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Mouse_Title">Mouse test</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Mouse_Text">Click, scroll and move to check buttons, the wheel, the polling rate and real DPI.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Reaction_Title">Reaction time</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_KbMouse_Reaction_Text">Wait for the screen to change, then click as fast as you can to measure your reaction time.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Clipboard_Pause_Title">Pause recording</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Clipboard_Pause_Text">Stops saving what you copy until you resume, for example while handling something private.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Search_Title">Search</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Search_Text">Type to filter your notes by title or text.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Pin_Title">Pin</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Pin_Text">Keeps the note at the top of the list.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Export_Title">Export</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Export_Text">Saves the note as a file.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Save_Title">Saved automatically</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_Notes_Save_Text">Changes are saved as you type; this shows the state.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Mirror_Title">Mirror</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Mirror_Text">Flips the picture like a mirror. It only changes the preview.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Preview_Title">Live picture</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Preview_Text">What the camera sees right now.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Snapshot_Title">Snapshot</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Snapshot_Text">Takes a picture of the current frame.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Readings_Title">Readings</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_WebcamTest_Readings_Text">The resolution, frame rate and brightness the camera is really giving.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Meter_Title">Level meter</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Meter_Text">Shows your voice level live. The marker holds the loudest point.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Readings_Title">Readings</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Readings_Text">The loudest peak, the quietest level and how many times the sound clipped.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Reset_Title">Reset</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Reset_Text">Clears the peak and counters to start measuring again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Timer_Title">Timer</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Timer_Text">Set the countdown time: 5:00, 90s, 1h30m or just 25.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Pomodoro_Title">Pomodoro</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Pomodoro_Text">Set work and break lengths and how many work sessions come before a long break.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Clock_Title">The clock</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Clock_Text">The time elapsed or left.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Lap_Title">Lap</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Lap_Text">Marks a lap without stopping the clock.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Reset_Title">Reset</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_TimerStopwatch_Reset_Text">Stops and clears the clock.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Find_Title">Find</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Find_Text">Looks through the folders you added for ones with nothing inside.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Select_Title">Select all or none</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Select_Text">Tick every empty folder, or clear the ticks.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Delete_Title">Send to the Recycle Bin</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_EmptyFolders_Delete_Text">Removes the ticked folders. They go to the Recycle Bin, so you can still restore them.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Details_Title">Your battery</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Details_Text">The battery bar fills as far as the battery's health and turns green, amber or red. Below it: design capacity against what it holds today, charge cycles and the rest.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Report_Title">Windows battery report</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_BatteryHealth_Report_Text">Makes Windows' own detailed battery report and opens it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_NowPlaying_Title">Now playing</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_NowPlaying_Text">The track that is playing, with its details.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Seek_Title">Seek bar</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Seek_Text">Drag to jump to another point in the track.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Play_Title">Play and pause</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Play_Text">Starts and pauses playback. Previous and next sit beside it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Volume_Title">Volume</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioReplay_Volume_Text">Sets how loud it plays.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryToggle_Title">Drives or History</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryToggle_Text">Drives shows each drive as it is now. History shows how its SMART numbers changed over time, with a chart and a table of readings.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryPick_Title">Choose what to look at</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryPick_Text">Pick a drive, a value such as temperature, reallocated sectors or life remaining, and the period. Press Record now to add a reading at once; refreshing Drive Health adds one too, at most every 6 hours.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryRecord_Title">Record now</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryRecord_Text">Reads every drive again and adds a reading even if the last one is recent.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryChart_Title">The trend</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryChart_Text">Red dots mark readings where a value that should stay low went up. A steady line is a healthy sign.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryReadings_Title">Every reading</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_DriveHealth_HistoryReadings_Text">Each reading with what got worse since the one before. Rising error counters mean the drive may be failing: back it up.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaHub_Modes_Title">Four pages in one</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MediaHub_Modes_Text">Mixed holds pictures, videos and music in one queue. Photos, Videos and Music are the full viewer, video player and audio player with all their options. Drop files anywhere and they jump to the page that fits.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Look_Title">Microphone type</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Look_Text">Pick the picture that matches your microphone: a stand, a handheld, a headset or earbuds. It only changes the drawing that fills with your voice.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Picture_Title">Your voice, as a picture</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_MicTest_Picture_Text">The microphone fills from the bottom as you get louder: green, amber near the top, red when it clips. The thin line marks the loudest point.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioOut_Look_Title">What you listen with</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioOut_Look_Text">Pick speakers, headphones, earphones or a headset. With two channels, the last three show a picture whose left and right sides fill with the sound each side plays.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioOut_Picture_Title">Left and right, as a picture</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Str_Tour_AudioOut_Picture_Text">Each side of the picture fills while that side plays. If one side stays empty during the channel test, that earcup or earbud is silent.</system:String>

